# Chess_core MCP

This repo has a project MCP server named `chess-core`. Use it before broad file search.

- `project_brief` / `search_docs` — architecture and onboarding facts. Do not reread all of `for_agent.me` unless the answer is still missing. `search_docs` also searches the mode rules catalog.
- `list_modes` / `mode_details` / `mode_docs` — mode ids **and rule descriptions**. `mode_details` returns live `GameMode` fields plus `rules`/`description`. `mode_docs` covers education-branch modes even when they are not registered on master. Do not guess how pieces move from tests alone.
- `legal_moves` / `apply_move` — real legality and FEN. Engine tokens look like `e2e4`, `P@e4`, duck `e2e4,e4e6`.
- `where_to_change` — put rules in `core`/`modes`, scenarios in `app`, I/O in `infra`, drawing in `ui`.
- `related_tests` / `check_layer_imports` — pick tests and keep `ui -> app -> core`.

Do not implement Capablanca 10x8, portals, or AlphaZero unless the user asks.
